input.description:
Follow-up from the MM-232 CodeRabbit review ([PR #122](https://github.com/malpercio-dev/ezpds/pull/122)).

`startSourceAuth` (and its sibling `startPdsAuth` in the claim flow) collapse **every** failure from `plugin:auth-session|start` into a single "cancelled" error:

```ts
// apps/identity-wallet/src/lib/ipc.ts — startSourceAuth
} catch {
  throw { code: 'SOURCE_AUTH_FAILED', message: 'auth session cancelled' } as MigrationError;
}
```

A genuine network failure or a malformed callback URL is therefore presented to the user as a *cancellation*, which misleads the retry UX in `MigrationSourceAuthScreen` (and the equivalent claim screen). The user is told they cancelled when the network actually dropped.

**Scope**
- Preserve/inspect the original rejection cause from the auth-session `start` call.
- Map genuine dismissal/cancellation to the "cancelled" case, and other errors (network, callback parse) to a more specific error so the screen can distinguish "you cancelled" from "something went wrong, retry".
- Apply to **both** `startSourceAuth` (migration) and `startPdsAuth` (claim) so the two flows stay consistent — this is why it wasn't fixed inside the MM-232 UI PR (`startSourceAuth` is unchanged code from #119, and `startPdsAuth` predates it; better to fix both wrappers together than diverge one).

**Refs**
- CodeRabbit comment on `apps/identity-wallet/src/lib/ipc.ts` (lines ~769–783) in PR #122.
- Deferred out of PR #122 with this rationale in the PR's disposition notes.

